# --- Evidence content -------------------------------------------------------
# Recording content never enters git: a repository cannot satisfy a retention
# obligation, and deleting a file does not delete the blob — it stays reachable
# by SHA in every clone, fork and CI cache. The repo holds CLAIMS about evidence
# (evidence/index.json); the content lives in the system of record that owns its
# lifecycle, reached through --evidence-root.
_evidence_root/
**/_evidence_root/

# ...with one deliberate exception. The worked example's evidence is synthetic
# demo text invented for this repository — no recording, no retention
# obligation, no classification. It is a TEST FIXTURE, and excluding it would
# make `make test` fail on a fresh clone, which is worse than the rule it would
# be enforcing. Real engagements live under engagements/ and are never exempt.
!example/_evidence_root/
!example/_evidence_root/**

# --- Build and tooling artefacts --------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.coverage
coverage.json
htmlcov/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.venv/
venv/

# --- Agent harness ----------------------------------------------------------
# `.claude/settings.json` and `.claude/hooks/` ARE committed: the SessionStart
# hook is what makes `make lint` and `make types` capable of running in a
# hosted session rather than silently skipping, and that belongs to the
# repository rather than to whoever happened to clone it.
# `settings.local.json` is the per-developer override and does not.
.claude/settings.local.json

# --- Local scratch ----------------------------------------------------------
*.tmp
*.log
.DS_Store
